text:
rachel: heads up — production alerts for function/tool-call validations just spiked. errors are all `STRUCTURED_OUTPUT_VALIDATION_FAILED` coming from the payments tool integration.
kevin: ugh. any sample payloads?
rachel: here's one from the logs: `tool_response: { "items": [ { "id": "sku-123", "amount_cents": 499 } ] }` — schema expects `items.[].price.amount` (number) and `currency` at items[].price.currency. validation error: "missing required property 'price' at /items/0"
maria: looks like the tool changed shape and our schema is strict. is this coming only from one model variant or across the fleet?
sam: telemetry shows ~1.8% of all tool calls failed in the last 5m, but mostly from region eu-west-1 and model variant `gptx-1.2-quant`. fallback routing kicked in for a subset.
rachel: right — routing_policy routed a small % to `gptx-1.2-compat` but it still returns old shape sometimes. leads to downstream lambda throwing 500s.
schema-bot: automated lint output attached: ```jsonschema
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "items": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["price"],
        "properties": {
          "price": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "amount": {
                "type": "number"
              },
              "currency": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
kevin: quick mitigation options: 1) runtime tolerant parser that maps amount_cents -> price.amount and defaults currency to USD, 2) temporary routing policy to send all calls to a stable variant, 3) bump SDK/tooling contract and force versioned tool call causing model to fail fast.
maria: I prefer 1 + 2 short-term. 3 will break a lot of customers if we flip contract server-side. can we implement tolerant parsing only for the payments-tool route and emit telemetry for all auto-mapped fields?
sam: yes — runtime can add a small transformer hook per-route. cost is tiny. we should also update console to display "schema auto-mapping rate" and a new alert if mapping rate > 0.5% per minute. that'll let us track regressions.
rachel: agreed. also need a rollout UX in console: when enabling tolerant parsing, show a canary slider and show pre/post expected schema mismatch delta. ops should be able to opt into auto-mapping per-namespace.
kevin: implementation note: transformer config could be a tiny jsonnet snippet attached to route: ```json
{
  "transformers": [
    {
      "match": "/payments.tools/*",
      "map": {
        "items[]:price.amount": "items[]:amount_cents / 100",
        "items[]:price.currency": "USD"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
schema-bot: added a ticket in #eng-platform backlog: infra-2041 (schema-mapping-for-payments-tool).
deploy-bot: canary rollout triggered: route=payments, variant=gptx-1.2-compat, pct=5, started by rachel at 1749123475.
maria: I'll own the runtime transformer PR. can someone add the console tile for schema-mapping metrics? Kevin?
kevin: on it — I'll add a per-route panel: schema.failures, schema.auto_mapped, schema.validation_latency and a small UX to toggle mapping with a warning modal.
sam: let's also emit a telemetry dimension for 'tool_signature_version' so we can correlate client versions with failures.
rachel: thanks. follow-ups: 1) runtime PR by EOD 2) console panel mock by tomorrow 3) escalation doc for customers impacted. I'll ping support to prepare a note. :thumbsup:
kevin: ack. creating dashboard card and config knobs.
maria: starting work now, will post WIP link.
sam: monitoring alert updated to fire if schema.failures > 0.5% for 2 consecutive 1m windows.
rachel: perfect. closing the loop — will post postmortem if anything else crops up.
